What’s Actually Inside renv.lock?
You don’t need to edit this file by hand, but it’s worth knowing what it contains:
{
  "R": {
    "Version": "4.6.0"
  },
  "Packages": {
    "dplyr": {
      "Package": "dplyr",
      "Version": "1.1.4",
      "Source": "Repository"
    }
  }
}
Every package your project depends on gets pinned to an exact version here. When a collaborator runs renv::restore(), R installs these exact versions — not whatever happens to be newest that day.


