if / else Conditionals
An if/else chain lets a function respond differently depending on the value it receives — only one branch runs, whichever condition is met first.






Note About This — Anatomy of if / else





if (condition1) {
  ... runs if condition1 is TRUE ...
} else if (condition2) {
  ... runs if condition1 was FALSE and condition2 is TRUE ...
} else {
  ... runs if nothing above was TRUE ...
}
Each condition must evaluate to a single TRUE or FALSE. R checks them in order and stops at the first one that’s TRUE — later branches are skipped entirely, even if they’d also have been TRUE.




