Your Turn: Add a Fifth Category
classify_expression() currently lumps everything above 10 into a single "detected" label. Modify it so counts above 1000 are labeled "high" instead, leaving "detected" for everything in between.

Please enable JavaScript to experience the dynamic code cell content on this page.


Check your work

classify_expression &lt;- function(count) {
  if (is.na(count)) {
    "missing"
  } else if (count == 0) {
    "not detected"
  } else if (count &lt; 10) {
    "low"
  } else if (count &lt;= 1000) {
    "detected"
  } else {
    "high"
  }
}
Note the order matters — the new branch has to come before the final else, and it has to use &lt;= for the upper bound of "detected" so the two categories don’t overlap or leave a gap at exactly 1000.

